==Strategy==
This stage takes a plethora of powerful Metal frontliners and pairs them up with Daboo of the Dead, a strong pusher that can repeatedly take down Anti-Metal stacks and gain ground easily with his Omni Attack. To make matters worse, most disposable [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] rely on chance and those that have atrociously slow attack rates or long recharge times will struggle immensely due to Daboo easily killing them, and it is very punishing if you mistime them.

This stage plays out as an endurance stage. Alongside the boss, there will be three waves of Metal pushers, the first wave containing Metal One Horns, the second containing a duo of Super Metal Hippoes and the third containing a lone Sir Metal Seal. Alongside this, the stage will constantly spawn Metal Doges. Your win condition is to hold off all three Metal waves, where maintaining as much ground as possible is crucial. Once the Metal waves have been fully exhausted, Daboo and the occasional Metal Doge are fairly easy to ward off and victory is generally secured. Of course, because of the infamously massive luck factor present on this stage, don't expect to beat it in one attempt.

The first Metal wave spawns right away. It is CRUCIAL that you try to take out the Metal One Horns as soon as possible, this will give you a headstart in cash and more importantly, will let you occupy as much ground as possible. Rapid attacking Critical Hitters like [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], or [[Rope Jump Cat (Rare Cat)|Noodle Cats]] are especially recommended since they let you brute force some of their health bars if crits are insufficient.

The second Metal wave is arguably the most dangerous. With a guaranteed chance to Knockback your cats, these Super Metal Hippoes push very aggressively. This wave is dealt with by timing [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]] and [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress/Soba Cat]] to avoid being hit by Daboo of the Dead, and helping them chip down at the Hippoes with their strong, guaranteed Critical Hits. The stronger and more consistent the Critical Hits, the better, as you can avoid making your units miss their attacks and drag out the wave far less.

Your success against the third and last Metal wave depends on how much ground you have held so far, and how much cash you've managed to save. In this wave, you simply time all your anti-Metal units and try to take the Sir Metal Seal down. If you have not lost too much ground, this Seal is surprisingly not a big issue.

Along the battle, the Metal Doges that spawn throughout are deceptively deadly and will be constant thorns on your side. They can walk up right after Daboo attacks and knocks out your frontline, causing you to lose space, especially if you have been playing carelessly. They could also shield the Super Metal Hippoes and Sir Metal Seal from your single-target Critical Hitters. Fast units like [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] are very useful for keeping ground here. You could time them such that they reaches the frontline right after Daboo of the Dead finishes his attack, keeping Daboo, the Metal Doges and other enemies in place, minimising space lost.

It is strongly recommended to attempt this stage after having completed Stories of Legend. Rock Cat and [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] are very strong cats to have against this stage, and the ability to boost your units past Lv.40 can be very helpful.

As for Cat Cannons, [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] is recommended, especially when upgraded to Lv.20+. It can provide large damage bursts to whittle Daboo, even if the Metals get in the way. Its knockback against Daboo can also interrupt his foreswing. With at least 10% max health damage, it can even finish Daboo off before he revives through its Soulstrike ability. If you do not have a high-leveled Holy Blast, the original Cat Cannon is a decent alternative, also being able to interrupt Daboo's foreswing and providing a small stun across the field. Alternatively, if somehow an upgraded Waterblast is available, it can be used instead to remove large portions of the Metals' HP, leaving them vulnerable to any critical hits connecting on them while other units defeat Daboo.

And while this stage is infamous for its RNG, remember that with good cat timings, you could make up for a lot of bad RNG.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]] - With decent speed, 5% critical chance and rapid area attacks, a well-timed Catyphoon can easily wipe out Metal Doges by its sheer weight of fire. If he does crit, he can even kill Metal One Horn, but he won't do much on Super Metal Hippoe and Sir Metal Seal, even being detrimental against Hippoe since his weak attacks will juggle them, causing your stronger attackers like Soba Cat to miss. Upgrading him to at least level 36 will allow him to survive at least one Daboo hit and continue to apply pressure.
*[[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] - Dealing heavy damage with guaranteed critical hits, Soba requires timing to compensate for her slow attack rate, recharge and foreswing, with successful hits easily removing Super Metal Hippoe and crippling Sir Metal Seal. At level 44, she can one-shot the Super Metal Hippoes. While Waitress Cat gets the job done, it is much harder to win the stage with her, as her damage will be lacking a lot and you'll have to take care to not be pushed back quickly before you can kill the Super Metal Hippoes or Seal.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Do not underlook this unit. As mentioned earlier, its fast speed and immovability makes it very great in stalling everything in this stage; you should most importantly send this unit out whenever Daboo kills your entire frontline.
*[[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Corrupted Moneko]] - Despite having an even longer animation than Soba with less damage, Crazed Moneko's guaranteed crit on third hit can still deal substantial damage to any Metal. Her [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]] combo with [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] boosts Critical Hit chance by 2%, which can greatly assist other lighter anti-metals. At level 37, she can survive a hit from Daboo. Additionally, by timing your Cat Cannon or Holy Blast, you could let her land another attack.
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] - With its Critical Hit Talent maxed and optionally Cost Down, this unit has an impressive attack rate for its 12% critical chance at a fairly low cost, allowing it to be accumulated and tear down the nasty Metals if given the chance. As a bonus, has a Research Combo with [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Cat]] if you happen to have a free slot.
*[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] - Though only available after clearing [[Charybdis' Mouth (Merciless)|Charybdis' Mouth]], Modern Cat's Resistance to Metals allow her to easily tank them for other units to land a hit on, neutralizing a majority of the pushing power on this level. If her True Form has been secured, it becomes even more cracked with its newfound Insanely Tough ability.
*[[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] - An unusual LD single target anti-Metal, Curry slows them for 1 second, and has a 8% critical chance. Combined with its respectable damage output, they can consistently delay the Metals until they or another unit land enough crits.
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] - Having Resistance to Zombies and Zombie Killer, Shigong retains its role as a meatshield and potential attacker against Daboo once the Metals dry up, as many anti-Metals and Holy Blast alone typically do it in.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - More of a gamble than gambit, large groups of Cameramen are absolutely required in addition to the critical talent (2%), the guaranteed Survivor Talent and any available Critical Hit Combos. A successful crit from even one can deal massive damage, second to only Soba out of all non-Uber units at equivalent levels. At Lv.69 (57 with maxed Attack Up Talent), one Cameraman crit does enough damage to instantly kill Super Metal Hippoe and shaves off more than a third of Sir Metal Seal's health. Start spawning her at the start of the stage to keep a stack going.
*[[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster & Charley]]: Extremely useful anti-metal CC who you'll mainly want to use to reduce the threat that Sir Metal Seal poses. While it has Single Target, it's much better of an option than other crowd control options such as [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoopmaster]] or [[Drumcorps Cat (Rare Cat)|Mochi]] due to his high speed allowing him to neutralize threats quicker.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] - Countering both the Metal One Horns in the start off with his disposable cheap cost and incredible speed, and the Metal Doges with his fast attack speed and decently reliable critical chance (6%), Cat Researcher can be a great pick for this stage if you really want a second rapid-attacking Critical Hitter. His fast speed can easily slip into Daboo's attack range and quickly pick off Metal Doges within Daboo's range, which can even occasionally clear your Soba's path to the Metal Hippoes or the Sir Metal Seal, and can be used as a substitute for Catyphoon whenever one is having financial problems beating this stage.
*[[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] - While mostly used as a throwaway meatshield and for his Combo, if you are really desperate to beat this stage, you could get his Critical talent, allowing him to greatly relieve the pressure exerted by the Metal Doges.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]] - Low cost, short recharge and high Critical Hit chance (50%) make Paladin an extremely effective anti-Metal Cat in spite of its low range. If boosted enough, Paladin can nearly one-shot the Super Metal Hippoes before they push too much and deal enough to knockback the Sir Metal Seal, making the rest of the stage fairly trivial.
*[[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sacred Blade Sakura]] - Sakura serves as a ranged tank with her Resistance against Metals, though her very low critical chance (5%) usually prevents her from outright killing them combined with her very slow attack rate. Her [[Part-Time Coworkers (Combo)|combo]] with Soba could give all units a small health boost, and in True Form, she gains a 1-slot combo for a 1% critical chance boost with the Insanely Tough ability for extra gravy.
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]] - Though not as consistent as Paladin (30%), Hayabusa's higher damage can greatly help against the stage's metal enemies, especially Super Metal Hippoe and Sir Metal Seal, eating up huge chunks of their HP.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] - As a Luga uber, Lufalan is a high-risk, high-reward unit who you'll usually only be able to see one attack out of. If you feel like gambling, Lufalan's Critical Hit can allow him to one-shot any threat of your choice before Lufalan dies, which will probably be Sir Metal Seal. Absolutely not a good choice by any means, but if you're struggling to think of other options for this level, Lufalan just might be your knight in shining armor.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Hades the Punisher]] - Great wall that can be very useful at stopping Daboo from advancing due to his extreme health and Daboo's slow attack rate. If you have him in [[True Form]], Super Metal Hippoe's knockback and Daboo's slow will not even work on him, though take care, as Metal Doge, Metal One Horn and Metal Seal can chip him down very fast. He has to directly tank all of their hits, therefore it's best to send him when you're sure the waves are in transition and have something that could kill off the Metals at hand.
*[[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]] - Nanaho has a 50% Critical chance on her second hit, and the Zombie Killer ability, both of which can be very useful in this stage.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss]] / [[Trickster Himeyuri (Uber Rare Cat)|Trickster Himeyuri]] / [[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)|Detective Vigler]] / [[Kaoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaolan Pasalan]] - All four of them have powerful Research combos, allowing you to send out your disposable anti-Metal units faster.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Sphinx Korps]] - Having resistance to Metals and Zombies allows it to tank significant amounts of damage from them and buy other units time to defeat said threats. Although Daboo is Immune to Weaken, the Metals are not. Super Metal Hippoe's Knockback can reset their attack animation, allowing them to Weaken the Metals more consistently, but can also cause all enemies to advance. With his True Form, his procs become more consistent with the Wave and he also gains Knockback, allowing him to retain ground easily.
*[[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Edgemaster Staal]] - If you have him, Edgemaster Staal can completely demolish the stage. He can permanently slow the Metals and dish out devastating Critical Hits, and he also packs Strong Against both the Metals and Daboo, giving him amazing stats against them.
*[[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao]] - If you're ''really'' that desperate, a high leveled Mighty Lord Gao has a 5% chance to one shot any of the metal enemies in the stage. He also has very good health, so he can survive multiple of Daboo's hits.

